0 FILE hogwarts-castle-v0.ldr
0 !BRICK_STATE {"schema_version":3,"status":"instruction_reconstruction_in_progress","version_label":"버전 0","reference_set":"LEGO Harry Potter Hogwarts Castle (71043)","source_manual_segments":["6590084-80.pdf","6590084-145.pdf","6607899-54.pdf","6607899-95.pdf","6607899-150.pdf","6607899-194.pdf","6607900-70.pdf","6607900-125.pdf","6607900-165.pdf","6607900-182.pdf","6607901-50.pdf","6607901-106.pdf"],"coverage":"6607901-50.pdf, booklet 22, printed pp.10–18 (steps 1–18) inspected as images. Root submodel hogwarts-frame.ldr has steps1–7. Local unplaced definitions: step8 partial with a 64179 ring, two 2420 corner plates, one 32278 rail, two 2780 pins and two 30000 end blocks; step14–15 with 32524/four pins/64179/32278; step17 with 64179/four pins. Steps9–13 and16 have not been reconstructed; step18 has a tentative independent beam-and-pin module. Circular builds on printed pp.6–9 remain separate.","piece_count":25,"placement_status":"Step8 partial local assembly now includes the frame, rail, pins, two 30000 end blocks, two corner plates, and a tentative 4032a/3700 center stack. Frame/rail and block/rail contacts have measured axes and insertion depths. The gray 1x2 illustrated side projection is not fully matched by 3700; its connector identity remains a candidate. Step14–15/17/18 are still unplaced; steps9–13 and16 remain to write.","validation":{"part_files":"shared LDraw shapes referenced","physical_fit":"Step1 four pins to root 64179: center/axis residual 0 LDU; adjacent beam/frame layers traverse 20-LDU layers. Step8 32278 body face meets the 64179 outer face at x=50; side-hole axes at x=50 and x=60 are collinear at z=±60 with 10-LDU separation along the axis. The two 2780 pins cross the seam. The 30000 end blocks at z=±140 have inward pin centers x=70 and axes collinear with rail holes centered x=60; each pin extends about 18.5 LDU into the rail's 20-LDU wall. Nominal body bounds meet at the x=70 plane; real friction/tolerance is untested. Other contacts remain provisional. The center 4032a/3700 candidate stack has a face/stud contact at y=-10; it is not proven to connect to the ring without its side pin.","full_manual_coverage":"in_progress","geometry_checks":"instance IDs, transforms, quantities checked locally; full validator requires catalog offer metadata not verified"},"steps":[{"pages":"10–12","steps":[1,7],"evidence":"Booklet 22 printed pp.10–12; existing root placements include the 64179 frame and step6–7 candidate pieces. See per-instance placement notes; several contacts remain provisional.","placement":"Root file hogwarts-frame.ldr; placed count 25."},{"pages":"13","steps":[8],"evidence":"Printed p.13 step8 parts and sequence: 64179 open-center 5x7 frame, 32278 long Technic rail, two 2780 pins, two purple 2420 corner plates, one lime 2x2 axle-hole plate, one gray 1x2 connector and two gray 2x2 side-pin connectors. Step1 inserts pins into the rail; step2 joins the frame; step3 turns the ring subassembly.","placement":"Local hogwarts-step8.ldr has frame 64179, two opposite-corner 2420 plates, 32278 rail, two 2780 pins, two 30000 end blocks, centered lime 4032a plate and gray 3700 brick candidate. Frame/rail axes at z=±60 are collinear with 10-LDU separation along X; two pins cross the seam. The built-in 30000 pins at z=±140 align with rail outer-face holes and insert ~18.5/20 LDU. 4032a studs meet the 3700 candidate base at y=-10, but the shown side projection remains unresolved. Partial and not root reachable."},{"pages":"17","steps":[14,15],"evidence":"Printed p.17 step14 makes a yellow 32524 beam with four 2780 pins; step15 adds a 64179 frame and 32278 long rail.","placement":"Local hogwarts-step14.ldr; seven physical references. Four frame/pin contacts align. Global placement is deferred pending confirmed relation to the root structure."},{"pages":"18","steps":[17],"evidence":"Printed p.18 step17 shows a 64179 frame with four 2780 pins.","placement":"Local hogwarts-step17.ldr; four pin axes align with the frame side holes. Global placement awaits a confirmed step16 joint."},{"pages":"18","steps":[18],"evidence":"Printed p.18 step18 callout shows one 90-degree gray L-shaped Technic beam and two pins. 32140 matches the visible 90-degree shape and candidate hole count, but no element number is printed.","placement":"Tentative local submodel hogwarts-step18.ldr: 32140 with 2780 pins in candidate holes (0,0,20) and (20,0,60). Axes/centers match the candidate DAT; part identity and selected holes remain uncertain. Not root reachable."}],"instances":[{"id":"part-0001","group":"frame","part":"32524.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":14,"position":[0,0,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Step 1 yellow Technic 7-hole beam; local origin centered; official 32524.dat has hole centers every 20 LDU along local Z and through-hole axes +Y. Manual orientation follows the horizontal callout."},{"id":"part-0002","group":"frame","part":"2780.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":0,"position":[0,10,-60],"matrix":[0,-1,0,1,0,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Step 1 pin at selected beam hole z=-60; beam hole axis R*(0,1,0)=(0,1,0); pin local X rotated to +Y. Origin at upper beam face y=10; nominal insertion span y=-8..10 (18 LDU) into 20-LDU beam thickness, leaving 2 LDU to far face; axial line and depth are separate checks."},{"id":"part-0003","group":"frame","part":"2780.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":0,"position":[0,10,-20],"matrix":[0,-1,0,1,0,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Step 1 pin at selected beam hole z=-20; beam hole axis R*(0,1,0)=(0,1,0); pin local X rotated to +Y. Origin at upper beam face y=10; nominal insertion span y=-8..10 (18 LDU) into 20-LDU beam thickness, leaving 2 LDU to far face; axial line and depth are separate checks."},{"id":"part-0004","group":"frame","part":"2780.dat","gobricks_id":